    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47912" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάσσω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾰάσσω</span></b>  (q.v.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sit, sit idle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατὸς δὲ θάσσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					391
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥσυχος θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				622
			</span></i> (troch.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφὶ βωμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					509
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἀκταῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					36
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίποδι ἐν χρυσέῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IT</u>
					1253
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς βάθροις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					715
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. sedis, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάσσειν θρόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					161
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. τρίποδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					91
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. δάπεδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					117
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. δυστήνους
				ἕδρας</span>
			<i>to sit</i> in wretched posture, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HF</u>
				1214
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				889
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾱσσω</span>
			
				contr.
			 fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαάσσω </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾰϝᾰκψω</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάβακος</span>): 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾶκος, θοάζω</span>
			.)</div>
